-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 2, §2.7 גננת שילוב
-- The integration kindergarten teacher: her unit of work, how far her
-- position may be split across days, her caseload, priority for completing
-- a position, her travel, splitting and preparation-hours allowances, the
-- education allowance, and age hours.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `2.7 גננת שילוב`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7/p2 The page's table of contents ("contents of the page").
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7/p3 Table of contents: 2.7.1.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7/p4 Table of contents: 2.7.6.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7/p5 Table of contents: 2.7.7.

§§ `2.7.1 Unit of work`

-- 1: a full position is 28 + 2 weekly hours — 28 with pupils and 2 of
-- guidance (הדרכה), 30 in all — and, beyond it, work with parents within two
-- "stay" hours.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_1
`weekly hours with pupils in a full position` MEANS 28
`weekly guidance hours in a full position` MEANS 2
`weekly hours in an integration teacher's unit` MEANS
    `weekly hours with pupils in a full position` PLUS `weekly guidance hours in a full position`
`weekly stay hours for work with parents, beyond the unit` MEANS 2

-- 2: the most days a week her position may be split across. The text gives
-- three bands: up to 1/3 (inclusive) two days; above 1/2 to 3/4 (inclusive)
-- four days; above 3/4 five days. Nothing is said for above 1/3 up to 1/2
-- (F-2.7-a): such a position has no maximum.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_2
DECLARE `days band` HAS
    `above`         IS A NUMBER  @desc the band holds fractions greater than this
    `up to`         IS A NUMBER  @desc and up to this, inclusive
    `most days`     IS A NUMBER

`the bands of 2.7.1.2` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_2/p2
        `days band` 0       (1/3) 2,
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_2/p3
        `days band` (1/2) (3/4) 4,
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_2/p4
        `days band` (3/4) 999   5

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `most days the table gives` f IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `most days`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD f GREATER THAN b's `above` AND f AT MOST b's `up to`) `the bands of 2.7.1.2`)

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `most days a week` f IS
    listToMaybe (`most days the table gives` f)

`a position between a third and a half has no maximum` MEANS
        `most days the table gives` 0.4 EQUALS EMPTY
    AND `most days the table gives` 0.5 EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `a position between a third and a half has no maximum`

-- ¶5: if the teacher agrees, she may be split further.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_2/p5
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, days IS A NUMBER, `she agrees to more splitting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the split is allowed` f days `she agrees to more splitting` IF
    `she agrees to more splitting` OR `within the maximum` (`most days a week` f) days

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER, days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the maximum` m days IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST most THEN days AT MOST most
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- 3: the number of children follows the number of kindergartens and her
-- weekly hours; at a full position (28 actual hours) 12-18 pupils in 3-5
-- kindergartens. ¶2's "detailed table" is a linked document, not in this
-- text, so the caseload at other positions is an input.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_3
GIVEN pupils IS A NUMBER, kindergartens IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a full position's caseload` pupils kindergartens IF
        pupils AT LEAST 12 AND pupils AT MOST 18
    AND kindergartens AT LEAST 3 AND kindergartens AT MOST 5

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_3/p2 Introduces the detailed caseload table, a linked document whose content is not in this text.

-- 4: a permanent integration teacher comes before any outside teacher for
-- completing her position.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_4
GIVEN `a permanent integration teacher in the system` IS A BOOLEAN, `an outside teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `comes first for completing a position` `a permanent integration teacher in the system` `an outside teacher` IF
    `a permanent integration teacher in the system` AND `an outside teacher`

-- 5: clauses 1-3 and 5 apply from 1.9.1981, clause 4 from 1.9.1982.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1__para_5
GIVEN clause IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `year clause 2.7.1 applies from` clause IS
    IF clause EQUALS 4 THEN 1982 ELSE 1981

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_1/p2 A source: director-general's circulars מב/6 and נח/9ב.

§§ `2.7.6.1 Travel allowance`

-- 1: with a car: paid for 200 km a month at the "global payment" rates,
-- pro-rated by position and period. 2: without a car: by report, up to
-- that sum. The per-km rate is an input.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_1__para_1
GIVEN `global-payment rate per km` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `share of the period worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly travel allowance with a car` `global-payment rate per km` `position fraction` `share of the period worked` IS
    200 TIMES `global-payment rate per km` TIMES `position fraction` TIMES `share of the period worked`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_1__para_2
GIVEN `reported travel cost` IS A NUMBER, `the car-owner's sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly travel allowance without a car` `reported travel cost` `the car-owner's sum` IS
    min `reported travel cost` `the car-owner's sum`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_1/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_1/p2 A source: special director-general's circular ה' 5739; circular נח/9ב.

§§ `2.7.6.2 Splitting allowance`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_2__para_1
GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the over-splitting allowance` kindergartens IF
    kindergartens AT LEAST 3

@desc The special allowance for over-splitting a position under section 1.11, given the number of kindergartens; an input until that section is imported
ASSUME `the splitting allowance of section 1.11` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_2/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_2/p2 A source: special director-general's circular ה' 5739; deputy director-general's circular of 25.8.80.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_2/p3 A source: director-general's circular מב/4, section 135ד.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_2/p4 A source: deputy director-general's circular of 19.1.82.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_2/p5 A source: director-general's circular נח/9ב.

§§ `2.7.6.3 Preparation hours`

-- 1: on top of her regular work she gets a supplement of preparation hours,
-- by this key. F-2.7-b: the unit of 2.7.1 already holds "2 guidance hours"
-- on top of the 28, 2.7.7 writes the full position as 28 "+ 2 preparation
-- hours", and this clause's own heading calls them counselling hours. The
-- reading adopted: they are one and the same two hours, so a full position
-- is the unit's 30 hours, not 32.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p1 akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p2
GIVEN `weekly hours worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `preparation hours` `weekly hours worked` IS
    BRANCH
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p3
        IF `weekly hours worked` AT MOST 10 THEN 0
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p4
        IF `weekly hours worked` AT MOST 19 THEN 1
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p5
        OTHERWISE 2

`hours paid for a full position if guidance and preparation are one` MEANS
    `weekly hours with pupils in a full position` PLUS `preparation hours` 28
`hours paid for a full position if they are two supplements` MEANS
    `weekly hours in an integration teacher's unit` PLUS `preparation hours` 28

`the unit's guidance hours and the preparation hours read as one or two` MEANS
        `hours paid for a full position if guidance and preparation are one` EQUALS 30
    AND `hours paid for a full position if they are two supplements` EQUALS 32
#ASSERT `the unit's guidance hours and the preparation hours read as one or two`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p6
`year the preparation-hours key applies from` MEANS 1980

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p7
`the key replaces every other procedure on preparation hours` MEANS TRUE

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p8 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p9 A source: director-general's circulars מא/3 and נח/9ב.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_3/p10 A pointer to section 4.6, the special-education supplement.

§§ `2.7.6.5 Education allowance`

-- "An integration kindergarten teacher (formerly a special-education
-- kindergarten teacher) is entitled to the education allowance. See section
-- 1.12." Section 1.12 is a named input. F-2.7-c: 1.12 itself excepts
-- integration kindergarten teachers from that allowance; this section's own
-- words are encoded.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_6_5/p1
`an integration teacher is entitled to the education allowance under 2.7.6.5` MEANS TRUE

@desc The education allowance of section 1.12 for the employee's salary; an input until section 1.12 is imported
ASSUME `the education allowance of section 1.12` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

-- The posts section 1.12 (¶33 of its rows) prints as excepted from the
-- class-education allowance, quoted here as the finding's evidence only.
DECLARE `kindergarten post` IS ONE OF
    `kindergarten teacher entitled to the coordination allowance`
    `assisting kindergarten teacher`
    `integration kindergarten teacher`
    `other kindergarten teacher`

`the kindergarten posts section 1.12 excepts, as printed` MEANS
    LIST `kindergarten teacher entitled to the coordination allowance`,
         `assisting kindergarten teacher`,
         `integration kindergarten teacher`

`2.7.6.5 grants what section 1.12 excepts` MEANS
        `an integration teacher is entitled to the education allowance under 2.7.6.5`
    AND elem `integration kindergarten teacher` `the kindergarten posts section 1.12 excepts, as printed`
#ASSERT `2.7.6.5 grants what section 1.12 excepts`

§§ `2.7.7 Age hours`

-- 1: the age-hours principle applies to her too: her position shrinks to
-- 26 (+2 preparation) hours with 2 age hours, to 24 (+2) with 4; with 4 she
-- works five days a week if she accepts it. 2: from 1.9.1981.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_7__para_1
GIVEN `age hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly hours with pupils after age hours` `age hours` IS
    `weekly hours with pupils in a full position` MINUS `age hours`

GIVEN `age hours` IS A NUMBER, `she accepts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `days a week with age hours` `age hours` `she accepts` IS
    IF `age hours` EQUALS 4 AND `she accepts` THEN JUST 5 ELSE NOTHING

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_7__para_2
`year age hours apply to integration teachers from` MEANS 1981

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_7/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_7__ssec_2_7_7/p2 A source: director-general's circular מב/6, section 223.

-- Worked examples; the per-km rate is a placeholder.
#ASSERT `most days a week` (1/3) EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `most days a week` 0.75 EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `most days a week` 0.8 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `the split is allowed` 0.6 5 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the split is allowed` 0.6 5 FALSE
#ASSERT `preparation hours` 15 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `weekly hours with pupils after age hours` 4 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `monthly travel allowance with a car` 2 0.5 1 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `monthly travel allowance without a car` 300 200 EQUALS 200
